From: Juanesf <juanesf91@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: sun60i-a733: fix SPI0 pinmux

The SPI0 pins on the A733 use pinmux 4 on the PC bank, the same value
the A523 uses for the same pins.  The current value 5 selects a
different function, which leaves MISO floating and makes the SPI NOR
probe fail with an all-zero JEDEC ID.

Signed-off-by: Juanesf <juanesf91@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -448,7 +448,7 @@
 			spi0_pc_pins: spi0-pc-pins {
 				pins = "PC2", "PC3", "PC4", "PC12";
 				function = "spi0";
-				allwinner,pinmux = <5>;
+				allwinner,pinmux = <4>;
 			};
 
 			spi1_ph_pins: spi1-ph-pins {
